.TH OZI-PKG 1 "2026" "OziOS" "OziOS commands"
.SH NAME
ozi\-pkg \- review software and install it the careful way
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ozi\-pkg
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ozi\-pkg
looks inside a package before it goes on the system, runs Debian and Ubuntu
packages and AppImages with only the permissions they are given, and builds
AUR packages in a throwaway container. A package that passes the review can
still be harmful; the review checks for known bad patterns only.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI review " file" " \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]"
Show what is inside a .deb, Arch package or AppImage and what deserves a look. Exit status 1 when something dangerous was found.
.TP
.BI install " file" " \fR[\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [rights]"
Install a .deb into its own rootless box, an AppImage in a sandbox, or an Arch package on the system.
.TP
.BI get " name..."
Install packages from the Arch repositories through the privileged helper.
.TP
.BI uninstall " name..."
Remove packages.
.TP
.BI aur " name..."
Resolve dependencies, review each recipe, build in a container and install the result.
.TP
.BI search " term"
Search the AUR.
.TP
.B upgrade
Update the whole system.
.TP
.BI undo " number"
Roll the system back to a snapshot.
.TP
.B list
List the boxed apps and sandboxed AppImages.
.TP
.BI perms " app" " \fR[rights]"
Show or change what an app may reach.
.TP
.BI run " app " "\fR[\fIarguments\fR]"
Start a boxed app.
.TP
.BI remove " app"
Delete the box of an app and its menu entries.
.SH RIGHTS
.TP
.B \-\-network\fR, \fB\-\-no\-network
Internet access.
.TP
.B \-\-files \fR\fInone\fR|\fIchosen\fR|\fIhome\fR
How much of the home folder is visible. \fB\-\-folder\fR \fIdir\fR adds a folder and implies \fBchosen\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu\fR, \fB\-\-sound\fR, \fB\-\-camera\fR, \fB\-\-devices\fR, \fB\-\-x11\fR, \fB\-\-nested\-sandbox
Graphics acceleration, sound, camera, USB and other devices, old-style display access, and apps that
bring a sandbox of their own. Each has a \fB\-\-no\-\fR form.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure or when the review found something dangerous.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ozi (1)
